# 🚀 Complete Git Guide for Kolhapur AI Community Contributors
Hey team! To help everyone learn real-world industry standards, we are upgrading our workflow. Our `main` branch is now reserved for the final, stable production code. All of our active building, testing, and collaborative enhancements will happen on the `dev` (development) branch.

Here is the exact step-by-step breakdown of how to sync your code, customize the project, and submit your features to get featured!


### Step 1: Clone the Repo and Switch to the Dev Branch
Run this once on your laptop to download the project and enter the development environment.

# 1. Clone the repository down to your computer
git clone https://github.com/kolhapuraicommunity/Kolhapur-Tourism-AI-Chatbot.git
cd Kolhapur-Tourism-AI-Chatbot

# 2. Switch your terminal directly to the dev branch
```
git checkout dev
```

* **Command 2:** Pull the absolute latest changes down from GitHub to your laptop.
  ```bash
git pull origin dev

```

> **Why do this?** If you don't pull the latest changes first, your code might conflict with a teammate's code later, causing messy errors.

---

### Step 2: Create Your Own Isolated Sandbox (Feature Branch)

Never write code directly on `dev` or `main`. Instead, create a temporary branch that acts as your personal scratchpad.

* **Command:** Create and immediately switch into a new branch. (Replace `yourname` with your actual name and use a hyphen).
```bash

```


git checkout -b feature/yourname-customization

```
  > **Why do this?** The `-b` flag tells Git to create a brand new branch. This keeps your experimental features completely hidden from everyone else until they are ready.

---

### Step 3: Add Your Customizations inside Your Folder
Open VS Code and check the `README.md` file in the main directory. We have listed a set of incredible system enhancements there that you can implement to level up this chatbot.

* Inside the project, look for the folder named `students/`.
* Find your personal folder (or create one named after yourself if you haven't already, e.g., `students/yourname/`).
* Place all of your script files, modifications, and experimental configurations **only** inside your own folder.
  > **Why do this?** This completely prevents two students from modifying the same file at the same time, ensuring nobody accidentally overwrites anyone else's hard work.

---

### Step 4: Take a Snapshot of Your Work (Stage & Commit)
Once your customized application runs successfully on your local laptop, it's time to lock it in and save your progress.

* **Command 1:** Stage all modified and new files so Git knows to track them.
  ```bash
git add .

```

* **Command 2:** Permanently save your changes on your machine with a clear description of what you customized.
```bash

```



git commit -m "Feat: Add yourname chatbot customization and enhancements"

```
  > **Why do this?** `git add .` gathers your files up, and `git commit` takes a permanent snapshot of them. Always write a meaningful commit message so the team knows what features you added!

---

### Step 5: Upload Your Branch to GitHub
Right now, your new branch and your changes only exist on your personal laptop. You need to push it online so the community can see it.

* **Command:** Push your unique branch up to the remote GitHub repository.
  ```bash
git push origin feature/yourname-customization

```

> **Why do this?** This safely uploads your personal branch to GitHub without touching the community's primary codebase.

---

### Step 6: Submit a Pull Request (PR) for Review

This asks the maintainer to review your code and combine it into the main development build.

1. Open our repository link in your web browser: `[https://github.com/kolhapuraicommunity/Kolhapur-Tourism-AI-Chatbot](https://github.com/kolhapuraicommunity/Kolhapur-Tourism-AI-Chatbot)`
2. You will see a yellow banner pop up at the top that says **"Compare & pull request"**. Click it!
3. **CRUCIAL SETTING:** Look at the branch dropdown options near the top left.
* Change the **base:** dropdown from `main` to **`dev`**.
* Leave the **compare:** dropdown set to your personal branch (`feature/yourname-customization`).


4. Type a short note summarizing your customization, then click the green **Create pull request** button.

---

### 🚀 Deploy, Share, & Get Featured!

Once your Pull Request is submitted and integrated, it's time to show the world what you built:

1. **Commit $\rightarrow$ Build $\rightarrow$ Deploy** your customized app to get your live application URL.
2. Share your live URL on **LinkedIn**!
3. Make sure to tag **#KolhapurAICommunity** in your post.

The **best and most unique customization** will be officially featured on the Kolhapur AI Community social handles! Let's keep building and shipping! 🚀
